00:02:47,317 --> 00:02:47,429
there.

67
00:02:48,263 --> 00:02:50,622
And then also an endpoint and you can keep

68
00:02:50,687 --> 00:02:52,083
the region set to auto.

69
00:02:52,612 --> 00:02:54,856
Unless you have more specific settings from

70
00:02:55,017 --> 00:02:56,026
AWS, for example.

71
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:00,499
So here to get the key ID and so on for

72
00:03:01,445 --> 00:03:04,939
R2, I'll go to Overview where I see all my

73
00:03:04,955 --> 00:03:05,356
buckets.

74
00:03:06,318 --> 00:03:08,915
And then here on the right, there is this

75
00:03:08,979 --> 00:03:11,383
Account Details area where I click on

76
00:03:11,512 --> 00:03:11,896
Manage.

77
00:03:12,473 --> 00:03:14,846
And there I can create a new account API

78
00:03:14,974 --> 00:03:18,757
token and I'll name that backup-course-demo.

79
00:03:20,024 --> 00:03:21,949
Of course, the name is up to you. You wanna

80
00:03:21,949 --> 00:03:24,884
set it to object read/write permissions.

81
00:03:25,718 --> 00:03:27,723
And of course you'll need to dive into the

82
00:03:27,723 --> 00:03:29,888
docs of the storage provider you may be

83
00:03:29,888 --> 00:03:32,358
using to find the right setup steps and

84
00:03:32,374 --> 00:03:34,507
permissions. Here are just the steps for

85
00:03:34,603 --> 00:03:35,518
Cloudflare R2.

86
00:03:36,624 --> 00:03:38,501
And then I wanna restrict it to just this

87
00:03:38,533 --> 00:03:38,886
bucket.

88
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:41,885
So to just backup-course-demo in my case.

89
00:03:42,703 --> 00:03:44,644
All the other settings are fine. I'll create

90
00:03:44,644 --> 00:03:47,098
that account API token. And now the values

